<title>MOROCCO: Morocco to float $13 mln consumer credit firm.</title>
<headline>Morocco to float $13 mln consumer credit firm.</headline>
<dateline>CASABLANCA 1996-11-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Morocco plans to float consumer credit firm CREDOR, worth 120 million dirhams ($13 million), on the Casablanca stock market on December 9, 1996, a bourse official said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Established in 1987 in Casablanca, Credit Domestic Rapide (CREDOR), has a capital of 120 million dirhams and expects a net profit of 55 million dirhams in 1996, the official said.</p>
</text>
